<BaseLayout
	title="About"
	description="Arnold Gamboa leads engineering teams, still ships code, and pastors LifeCity Church in Pasig City — 25 years of making technology useful, without treating faith as a side note."
	path="/about/"
>
	<article class="page">
		<h1>About</h1>
		<p class="page__lede">
			I lead engineering teams, still write software, and pastor a local church. Those are not
			three brands. They are one life, from Pasig City.
		</p>

		<h2>Making technology useful</h2>
		<p>I have spent 25 years making technology useful.</p>
		<p>
			I have built automation for clients across different business environments. A system only
			matters if it holds up in real work: it has to be reliable, handle exceptions, protect
			sensitive access, and stay understandable.
		</p>
		<p>
			I still work that way. I learn how a place actually runs, I build what it needs, and I stay
			close to it after it is live. That has been true in client work, in leading engineering
			teams, and now in{' '}
			<a href="https://aiforreal.work" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AI for Real Work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>LifeCity Church</h2>
		<p>
			I pastor{' '}
			<a href="https://lifecity.ph" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LifeCity Church</a>
			{' '}in Pasig City, where I live.
		</p>
		<p>
			It is a small Christian church. On Sundays we gather at the Goodyear Center in Kapitolyo.
			Through the week it looks more like coffee, homes, and the same people showing up for each
			other. I know the room. I know the names. That is the work I do not want to outsource.
		</p>
		<p>
			Pastoring is not a side project next to software. It is part of how my week is actually
			spent — sermons, people, the slow parts of ministry that should stay slow. Faith and
			technology both belong there. Neither is a footnote.
		</p>

		<h2>What I’m building</h2>
		<p>
			<a href="https://youpastor.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">YouPastor</a>
			{' '}is an AI workspace for pastors, grown out of that same conviction: tools should carry
			the repetitive drag without taking the judgment that belongs to a person.
		</p>
		<p>
			If you want the current season, that’s on <a href="/now/">Now</a>. If you want to write,{' '}
			<a href="mailto:arnold@gamboa.ph">email me</a>.
		</p>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>
